Education are statutory \nautonomous organizations established under respective Central Acts of Parliament and governed \nby provisions of the Acts/ Statutes/ Ordinances/ Regulations made thereunder. Occurring of \nvacancies and filling thereof is a continuous process. The vacancies arise due to retirement, \nresignation and additional requirements on account of enhanced students’ strength. \nMinistry of Education has directed all the Central Higher Educational Institutions (CHEIs) to fill \nup the vacancies in Mission Mode, including a special drive for reserved category posts. As on \n03rd August, 2023, a total of 13371 vacancies have been filled up in the CHEIs under the Mission \nRecruitment drive, in a period of ten months only. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|STARRED   |243", "t": "Decriminalisation of Compoundable Offences under Companies Act, 2013", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \nDEPARTMENT OF PHARMACEUTICALS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 243 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21st July, 2023 \n  \nPromotion of JAKs  \n \n243. SHRI RAJENDRA DHEDYA GAVIT:  \n \nWill the Minister of CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has any plan to promote Janaushadhi Kendras (JAKs) among the \npeople since the cost of medicines available in such outlets are priced 50 to 90 percent less than \nthe branded medicines, if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) the measures taken to ensure that Government and private medical practitioners prescribe \nthe medicines as per their chemical composition and not by branded names;  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to increase the number of Janausha dhi Kendras by \nissuing licences to qualified persons and extending bank loans to ensure that generic medicines \nare available with much greater ease, if so, the details thereof; and  \n(d) whether the Government proposes to add more generic medicines and equi pment for sale \nfrom Janaushadhi Kendras and if so, the details thereof?  \n  \nANSWER \n  \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF CHEMICALS AND FERTILIZERS \n         (SHRI BHAGWANTH KHUBA)   \n        \n(a):  In order to promote of Pradhan Mantri Bhartiya Janaushadhi Pariyojana (PMBJP), the \nDepartment of Pharmaceuticals and Pharmaceuticals & Medical Devices Bureau of India \n(PMBI), the implementing agency of the Scheme periodically requests State /UT Governments/ \ndistrict administrations to create awareness about the sc heme. PMBI also spreads awareness \nabout the scheme through advertisements in Print Media, Radio, TV, cinema, outdoor publicity \nas well as through social media.  Further, Jan Aushadhi Diwas is celebrated every year on 7 th \nMarch for further dissemination and spreading awareness about the scheme.  \n \n(b): Clause 1.5 of Indian Medical Council (Professional Conduct, Etiquette and Ethics) \nRegulations, 2002 prescribes that every physician should prescribe drugs with generic names \nlegibly and preferably in capital letters and he/she shall ensure that there is a  rational \nprescription and use of drug. In order to encourage doctors to prescribe generic medicines, the \nDepartment of Pharmaceuticals periodically requests the Ministry of Health & Family Welfare \nto direct the Government doctors to prescribe generic medicines only.  \n  \n(c):  A target to open 10,000 Jan Aushadhi Kendras by  31.03.2024 has been kept. In order to \nencourage people for opening the PMBJKs, Government provides an incentive up to Rs. 5.00 \nlakh @ 15% of monthly purchases made, subject to a ceiling o f Rs. 15,000/ - per month. In \naddition, one-time additional incentive of Rs. 2.00 lakh is provided to the Kendras opened in \nNorth-Eastern States, Himalayan areas, Island territories and backward areas mentioned as \n\naspirational district by NITI Aayog or open ed by women entrepreneur, ex - serviceman, \nDivyang and SCs & STs.  \n  \n(d): The product basket of PMBJP presently comprises of 1,800 medicines and 285 surgical \ndevices. The same is reviewed periodically by PMBI and new medicines and surgicals are \nadded to the basket.  \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|STARRED   |244", "t": "Reforms in EPF and ESI", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n� \n���������  \n��������������������������  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.07.2023 \n� \n������������������������������  \n� \n244.     MS. MIMI CHAKRABORTY: \n���������������������������������������������������������������������� \nWill the Minister of WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n                           \n(a) the details of disbursement of funds to Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana \n(PMMVY), the maternity benefit programme in the country during the last four \nyears State-wise; \n(b) whether all the beneficiaries have received the financial benefit of Janani \nSuraksha Yojana therein; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) the number of Anganwadi Centres/approved  health centres working in the \ncountry, State-wise? \n  \n  \n������  \n� \nMINISTER FOR WOMEN AND CHILD DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRIMATI SMRITI ZUBIN IRANI) \n� \n \n(a)        The State-wise details of Central share of funds released during the last four \nyears under Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana (PMMVY) is at Annexure-I. \n  \n(b) & (c)          All beneficiaries of PMMVY are not eligible for receiving maternity benefit \nunder Janani Suraksha Yojana (JSY). However, State-wise number of beneficiaries who \nhave received maternity benefit under JSY as reported by States/UTs on Pradhan Mantri \nMatru Vandana Yojana-Common Application Software (PMMVY-CAS) is at Annexure-II. \n  \n(d)       The State -wise number of Anganwadi Centres working in the country is at \n�������� ������\n  \n  \n  \n*****  \n  \n� �\n\n�������� �� \n� \n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� ���� ������� ��� ����������� ������� ��� ���� ����� ������������ ����������\n�