ad": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nADMITTED STARRED QUESTION NO. *68 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25th July, 2023 \n \nRASHTRIYA KAMDHENU AAYOG \n \n*68 . MS LOCKET CHATTERJEE  \n        SHRIMATI NAVNEET RAVI RANA \n \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nमत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री \n be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the aims and objectives of establishing Rashtriya Kamdhenu Aayog (RKA) and \nthe achievements made so far since its inception; \n \n(b) the details of the works done for conservation and enhancement of indigenous \nbreeds of cows in the country under the Rashtriya Gokul Mission during the last three \nyears, State-wise; \n \n(c) the number of Gokul Grams sanctioned in West  Bengal, Madhya Pradesh, \nMaharashtra particularly in Amravati and Bihar under the said mission; \n \n(d) whether the Government proposes to increase the number of Gokul Grams \nthereunder and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the steps taken by the Government for the  protection and development of the \nlivestock population as well as for the conservation of indigenous breeds in the country? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n(Shri Parshottam Rupala) \n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *68 RASHTRIYA KAMDHENU AAYOG TO BE \nANSWERED ON 25th July 2023.  \n \n(a) The Rashtriya Kamdhenu Aayog  (RKA) was constituted vide Resolution No. 3 -\n260/2019-AHT (RGM) dated 21st February, 2019 as an Advisory body and as an \nintegral part of Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM). \n \nRKA was constituted for the purpose of conservation, protection and development of \ncows and their progeny. It was assigned to develop policy frame work and shape \nguidelines aimed at formulat ing policy to provide direction to the implementation of \nschemes related to cattle genetic up-gradation of genetic resources. \n \nThe members of the RKA vis ited Gaushala, Stray Cattle homes etc in the country for \nconsultative meetings. Also conducted several meetings with Hon’ble Governor, AH \nMinisters, Universities, Gau sewa Aayogs of States etc. and discussed on related \nissues. The members of RKA visited ac ademic institutions and universities and had \ninteraction about the cows and its development with regard to scientific, economical, \nenvironmental, spiritual aspects. \n \n(b) The details of work done for conservation  and  enhancement of Indigenous breed of \ncows in the country under Rashtriya Gokul Mission (RGM) state-wise during last 3 years \nis at Annexure-I. \n \n(c) & (d) Following is the details of the Gokul Grams sanctioned u nder Rashtriya Gokul \nMission in the State of Bihar, Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra and West Bengal:   \n \nState  No of Gokul Gram \nsanctioned \nLocation of Gokul Gram \nBihar 1 Dumraon,  Buxar \nMadhya Pradesh 1 Ratona, Sagar \nMaharashtra 2 Pohara, Amravati \nTathawade, Pune \nWest Bengal - No proposal was received from the State \n \nAs per the revised and realigned guidelines of Rashtriya Gokul Mission for 2021-2022 to \n2025-2026, the component has been discontinued under the scheme.  However, \nGovernment of India is undertaking establishment of breed multiplication farms \npreferably of indigenous breeds and under the component 50% capital subsidy is \navailable for entrepreneurs  (Individual / Self Help Groups/Farmer Cooperative \norganizations / Farmer Producer organizations /Joint Liability Groups and section 8 \ncompanies). \n  \n\n(e) Following major steps have been undertaken by Government of India for the \ndevelopment and conservation of indigenous breeds: \n \n(i) Nationwide AI porogramme  for extension of Artificial Insemination coverage  \n \n(ii) Progeny testing and pedigree selection for product ion of high genetic merit bulls  \nof indigenous breeds.  \n \n(iii) Establishment of Breed Multiplication Farms preferably of indigenous breeds  \n \n(iv) Promotion of In-vitro Fertilization (IVF) technology for faster genetic up gradation \nof indigenous breeds  \n \n(v) Implementation of genomic selection using genomic chip.  \n \n(vi) Sex sorted semen production for indigenous breeds  \n \n(vii) Funds have been released to the States for establishment of 16 Gokul and 2  \nNational Kamdhenu Breeding Centres. \n\nAnnexure-I \nState-wise achievements made under Rashtriya Gokul Mission for Development and conservation of \nIndigenous breeds \nSN Name of \nState \nPedigree \nSelection \nProgramm\ne \nProgeny \nTesting \nNo. of \nGokul \nGrams   \nNo. of \nNational \nKamdhe\nnu \nBreeding \nCenter \nIVF \nLabs \nNationwide AI programme (NAIP) \nAnimal \nCovered \nAI done Farmers \nbenefitted \n1 Andhra \nPradesh \n-  1 1 1 2 4122110 5842406 2244607 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh \n-    1   - 3187 3332 1527 \n3 Assam  -       - 1014449 1159717 869352 \n4 Bihar  -   1   2 2130026 2483141 1691520 \n5 Chhattisgarh  -   1   1 1349355 1566516 863260 \n6 Goa "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|STARRED   |69", "t": "Veterinary Health Services", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 69\n(To be answered on the 20th July 2023)\n \nUDAN SCHEME FOR UTTAR PRADESH\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) whether the Government has set the target of connecting 1000 routes of air\nconnectivity by 2026 under UDAN Scheme and if so, the number of routes\nthat would get connected in Uttar Pradesh along with the number of Airports\nthat would startfunctioning by 2026; and\n(b) whether the number of passengers flying through aeroplane have\nincreased due to UDAN Scheme and if so, the details thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of State in the Ministry of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a): Yes Sir. The number of routes awarded and valid in the state of Uttar\nPradesh upto the last round of bidding under the scheme is 273 , out of which\n59 UDAN routes in Uttar Pradesh have been operationalised as on 12.07.2023.\nUDAN 5.0 round has been launched on 21.04.2023 to identify additional\nroutes to connect underserved and unserved airports across the country,\nincluding the State of Uttar Pradesh\n \nEighteen (18) RCS airports namely Agra, Aligarh, Prayagraj, Bareilly,\nKanpur, Chitrakoot, Ayodhya, Ghazipur, Jhansi, Moradabad, Kushinagar,\nMeerut, Muirpur, Azamgarh, Shravasti, Saharanpur, Hindon and Fursatganj\nhave been identified for development under various rounds of bidding in\nUttar Pradesh. RCS Flights operation from Agra, Prayagraj, Bareilly,\nKanpur, Hindon and Kushinagar have already commenced. The remaining\nAirports are at various stages of development.\n \n \n(b): More than 1.23 crores passengers have travelled on RCS UDAN flights\nsince the inception of the scheme\n \n69. SHRI JAGDAMBIKA PAL\n be pleased to state:-\n (GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD))\n\n \n*****"}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|STARRED   |7", "t": "Solar Street Lights under AJAY", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 \nANSWERED ON 20.07.2023 \n \nSOLAR STREET LIGHTS UNDER AJAY \n*7. SHRI GAURAV GOGOI \n \nWill the Minister of NEW AND RENEWABLE ENERGY be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware of the fact that over 1.35 lakh solar street lights were \ninstalled against sanction of around 1.45 lakh lights in Phase-I of the Atal Jyoti Yojana \n(AJAY) and over 1.37 lakh such lights were installed against sanction of around 1.50 lakh \nlights under Phase-II of the scheme; \n(b) if so, the reasons for incomplete installation of targeted solar street lights in both the \nphases of AJAY therefor; \n(c) whether the Government proposes to launch Phase-III of AJAY; \n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the likely date of launch and target set thereunder; \nand \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF NEW & RENEWABLE ENERGY AND POWER  \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n(a) to (e) A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. 07 \nto be answered on 20.07.2023 regarding Solar Street Lights under AJAY \n \n(a) & (b ) The Phase-I of Atal Jyoti Yojana (AJAY) was launched in September 2016 for \nimplementation upto 31.03.2018. Till 31.3.2018, sanctions were issued by respective District \nMagistrates (DMs) for installation of around 1.45 lakh solar street lights (SSLs) by utilising \nMPLADS Fund under AJAY Phase-I. However, within the timelines allowed for installation \nof SSLs, a total of around 1.35 lakh SSLs could be installed.  \nSimilarly, t he Phase-II of Atal Jyoti Yojana (AJAY) was launched in December 2018 for \nimplementation within a period of one year, which was later extended till 31.3.2021. However, \ndue to outbreak of COVID-19, the Government had suspended MPLADS Fund for two years \ni.e. for FY 2020-21 and FY 2021-22 and accordingly, the AJAY Phase-II, which was partially \nfunded through MPLADS Fund, was discontinued w.e.f. 01.04.2020 for new sanctions.  \nTill 31.3.2020, sanctions were issued by respective DMs for installation of around 1.50 lakh \nsolar street lights (SSLs) by utilising MPLAD Fund under AJAY Phase -II. Considering the \nCOVID-19 restrictions and supply chain issues, the installation of sanctioned quantity of SSLs \nwere first extended till 31.12.2021 and thereafter, finally extended till 30.6.2022. Within the \nextended period, around 1.37 lakh SSLs were reported installed under AJAY Phase-II.  \nThe major reasons reported by EESL, the implementing agency for the scheme, for incomplete \ninstallations, include delay in confirmation of sites where the SSLs were to be installed, and \ndelay in release of funds from MPLADS Fund, etc. \n(c) to (e ) Presently, there is no proposal to launch AJAY Phase-III scheme. H owever, a \nproposal, including for providing solar street lights on the similar lines of AJAY, is under \nconsideration of Ministry of New and Renewable Energy. \n**** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|STARRED   |70", "t": "Beneficiaries under PMAY-G", "head": "������������������� �\n�������� ��������� �\n�\n��������� �\n���������������������� �� �\n������������ ���������� �\n�\n��������������������������������� �\n�\n����� ������������������������ �\n�\n� �������������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������� ���������������������\n��� ����������������������� �\n�\n����� ���� ������� ��� �������� ������ ��������� � ���������� ����� ���\n���������� ������� ���� ����� ��� ������� ���� ���� ������� ��� �����������\n�������� �������������������������������������������������� ������������\n������������ �\n�\n����� ����������������������������������������� �������������������������\n���������� ��������� ����������� � ��������� ��� ���� ����������� ������\n���������� �\n�\n����� �������������������������������� �\n�\n����� �������������������������������������������� ��������������������\n���������������������� ��������� �\n�\n����������� �\n�\n������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����������������� �\n�\n������ � ��������������������������������������������������������\n������ ����������� ���� ���� �������� ��� ������ ���������� ����������\n������������������������������������� ����\n�������������\n�\n\n������\n�������� ��� �������� ��� �������� ������ ���������� ����������\n�������������� ����������� ����� ����� ���������� ������� ���� ����� ����\n������ �\n�\n������� ���� ����� ������� � ���� ���� ����������� ����������\n�������������������������������������������������� ���� �\n�\n����� ���� �������� ��� ����������� ������ �������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������\n����� ������ ���� ����� ����� ������ ��� �������� ��������� ���� ��� � ����