4 351790 358499\n30 Patan 362556 385601 377782 374176 369215 363345 251139 336471\n31 Porbandar 140239 139746 138538 136602 132793 135219 88550 94208\n32 Rajkot 424726 412519 395937 403133 410056 416031 292867 425982\n33 Rajkot Corp 273442 282480 285731 304467 319173 314043 204375 312296\n34 Sabarkantha 386707 398797 387583 387720 409966 399170 284594 351798\n35 Surat 380632 381286 378073 382596 436472 454974 159905 433157\n36 Surat Corp 1022677 1002948 1016303 1039404 1088796 1090659 779963 879833\n37 Surendranagar 422223 426169 421756 414141 417368 415966 297918 336014\n38 Tapi 183157 192255 183855 182909 168435 191833 126853 175920\n39 V adodara 322684 314875 308324 313856 325675 327687 245992 "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|UNSTARRED |362", "t": "Ayurvedic Hospitals in Haryana", "head": "1\nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF AYUSH\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.362\nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST JULY,2023\nAYURVEDICHOSPITALS IN HARYANA\n†362. SHRI NAYABSINGH:\nWill the Minister of AYUSH be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of Ayurvedic hospitals functioning in the country particularly in Haryana and\nKurukshetra Parliamentary Constituency;\n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise;\n(c) whether the Government has any plan to set up AYUSH Hospitals in each district of the\ncountry particularly in Haryana and Kurukshetra Parliamentary Constituency;\n(d) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise; and\n(e) the measures taken/proposed to be taken by the Government to set up more AYUSH\nHospitals in the country?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF AYUSH\n(SHRI SARBANANDA SONOWAL)\n(a) & (b) The number of Ayurvedic Hospitals functioning State/UT-wise in the country including\nHaryana is furnished at Annexure-I. Further, 1 (one) Ayurvedic hospital is functioning in\nKurukshetra district.\n(c) to (e) Public Health being a State subject, setting up of Ayush Hospitals in any district of any\nState/UT, comes under the purview of respective State/UT Governments. However, under\nCentrally Sponsored Scheme of National Ayush Mission (NAM), there is a provision of financial\nassistance to States/UTs for setting up of 50/30/10 bedded integrated Ayush hospitals.\nAccordingly, State/UT Governments including Haryana may avail financial assistance by\nsubmitting suitable proposal through State Annual Action Plan (SAAP) as per the provision of\nNAM guideline. Further, as per the proposals received from the State/UT Governments including\nHaryana, the status of approved integrated Ayush Hospitals for setting up in the country is\nfurnished as Annexure-II.\n\n2\nAnnexure-I\nThe number of Ayurvedic Hospitals functioning State/UT-wise (as on 01.04.2021)\nS. No. State / UT No. of Ayurvedic Hospitals\n1 Andhra Pradesh 3\n2 Arunachal Pradesh 10\n3 Assam 1\n4 Bihar 5\n5 Chhattisgarh 11\n6 Delhi 2\n7 Goa 1\n8 Gujarat 39\n9 Haryana 13\n10 Himachal Pradesh 33\n11 Jammu & Kashmir 4\n12 Jharkhand 0\n13 Karnataka 193\n14 Kerala 129\n15 Madhya Pradesh 41\n16 Maharashtra 78\n17 Manipur 6\n18 Meghalaya 4\n19 Mizoram 1\n20 Nagaland 2\n21 Odisha 6\n22 Punjab 21\n23 Rajasthan 118\n24 Sikkim 2\n25 Tamil Nadu 2\n26 Tripura 3\n27 Uttar Pradesh 1788\n28 Uttarakhand 431\n29 West Bengal 6\n30 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 1\n31 Chandigarh 1\n32 Dadra & Nagar Haveli and Daman & Diu 2\n33 Ladakh 0\n34 Lakshadweep 1\n35 Puducherry 1\n36 Telangana 4\nTotal 2963\n\n3\nAnnexure-II\nState/UT wise status of integrated Ayush hospitals approved from 2014-15 to 2022-23\nSl. No. State/UT Location\n1. Andaman & Nicobar Islands Port Blair\n2. Andhra Pradesh Kakinada\nVisakhapatnam.\n4. Arunachal Pradesh Bhalukpong New\nLikabali New\n6. Assam\nGoalpara\nMajuli\nKokrajhar\nBaksa\nMorigaon\nKaliabor\nDiphu\nBajali\n14. Bihar Patna\n15. Chandigarh Chandigarh\n16. Chhattisgarh\nJangir Champa\nMahasamund\nKoria\nKorba\nKanker\nNarayanpur\nBijapur\nDantewada\nDalli Rajhara\n25. Goa South Goa\nNorth Goa\n27. Gujarat Surat\n28. Haryana Hisar\n29. Himachal Pradesh Kullu\nMandi\n31. Jammu & Kashmir\nKishtwar\nKup