dia publishers in the Government’s inter -ministerial panel that is \nmeant to help bolster the draft Digital Competition Act ?  \n\nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING; AND \nMINISTER OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS  \n(SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR) \n(a) to  (c): Ministry of Corporate Affairs has informed that they have \nconstituted a Committee on Digital Competition Law having \nrepresentatives from Ministry of Electronics & Information \nTechnology, Department of Economic Affairs, Department of \nCommerce, Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal \nTrade, Department of Consumer Affairs & NITI Aayog to review \nexisting provisions in Competition Act, 2002 and the rules and \nregulations framed thereunder and to examine whether they are \nsufficient to deal with the challenges that have emerged from the \ndigital economy and related matters. \nThe Digital News Publishers Association and News  Paper \nAssociation of India have been invited to make presentations and \nsubmissions before the Committee. \n***** \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|17|12|UNSTARRED |768", "t": "National Programme for Dairy  Development", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.768 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 25TH JULY, 2023 \n \nNATIONAL PROGRAMME FOR DAIRY DEVELOPMENT \n \n768. SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY: \n  \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING  \nमत्स्यपाऱन, पशुपाऱन और डेयरी मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) the details of State Cooperative Dairy Federations, District Cooperative Mild Producers Union, \nSelf Help Groups (SHGs) in the country, State/UT-wise including Saran district of Bihar;  \n(b) the funds released under the National Programme for Dairy Development  during the last three \nyears, State/UT-wise including Saran district of Bihar;and \n(c) thenumber of projects and proposals received and sanctioned thereunder,State/UT -wise \nincluding Bihar? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY AND DAIRYING \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA) \n \n(a) State/UT-wisedetails of number of State Cooperative Dairy Federations , District Co operative \nMilk Producers Union & Self Help Groups (mobilised under DeendayalAntyodayaYojana-National \nrural Livelihood Mission(DAY-NRLM) in the country is at Annexure-I.In Saran District of Bihar, \n32813 number of SHGs are mobilized under (DAY-NRLM) \n(b)State/UT-wise funds released including Saran district of Bihar under the National Programme for \nDairy Development during the last three years is at Annexure-II. \n(c) State/UT-wise number of project proposals received andsanctioned by the Department under \nNPDDscheme is at Annexure-III. \n \n \n \n**** \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nDetails of state/ UT wise State Cooperative Dairy Federations and District Cooperative Milk \nUnions in the country is as under:- \n \nS. No. State/ UT \nState Dairy \nFederations/ Apex \nBodies* \nMilk Unions* \nSHGs formed \nunder DAY-\nNRLM# \n1 Andaman 0 0 1199 \n2 Arunachal 0 0 8197 \n3 Andhra Pradesh 1 3 853158 \n4 Assam 0 3 344109 \n5 Bihar 1 9 1096939 \n6 Chhattisgarh 1 0 263465 \n7 Daman DIU & NH 0 0 956 \n8 Goa 1  0 3659 \n9 Gujarat 1 22 271941 \n10 Haryana 1 6 57625 \n11 Himachal Pradesh 1 3 42691 \n12 Jammu & Kashmir 1 2 81797 \n13 Jharkhand 1  0 279334 \n14 Karnataka 1 15 276655 \n15 Kerala 1 3 254902 \n16 Ladakh 0 0 585 \n17 Lakshadweep 0 0 328 \n18 Madhya Pradesh 1 6 443737 \n19 Maharashtra 1 28 599750 \n20 Manipur 0 1 7756 \n21 Meghalaya 0 4 43971 \n22 Mizoram 0 4 9574 \n23 Nagaland 1 3 14283 \n24 Odisha 1 12 530577 \n25 Puducherry 0 1 4412 \n26 Punjab 1 11 41005 \n27 Rajasthan 1 24 309955 \n28 Sikkim 0 2 5699 \n29 Tamil Nadu 1 27 321687 \n30 Telangana 1 2 439672 \n31 Tripura 0 2 48881 \n32 Uttar Pradesh 1 20 722032 \n33 Uttarakhand 1 13 57627 \n34 West Bengal 1 14 1075991 \n  TOTAL 22 240 8514149 \nSource: *NDDB, #Department of Rural Development \nDAY-NRL